d inputs, not events caused by your drafts.\\n\\n\\nObtain the five native source locations through the interview. Inputs include searchable PDFs, a Google Sheets workbook and a Notion page; business data is not bundled in the starter. Every new run must attempt fresh reads of all five locations through a browser or supported API/export route. Retain the complete relevant content actually used, including its original wording, identities, precision and history, and bind it in `sources.json`. Preserve the supplied case clock and arrival boundaries. Record inaccessible, partial or incompatible content and its affected scope explicitly. A URL, successful response or hash alone is not evidence of complete access. Do not alter sources or silently substitute bundled inputs, earlier downloads or an AI paraphrase. A labelled offline replay may reuse an earlier run's retained inputs without claiming fresh access.\\n\\nPeople retain business approval, exception and payment authority. The Skill prepares local work, validates and consumes authorized scenario decisions, and records their effects; it must not fabricate a reply, make professional approval recommendations, send real requests, book travel or move money..\\n\\nIn your captured coding conversation, make and explain four source-grounded choices: how incomplete claims affect independent work; which work to revalidate after material corrections; the financial-completion conditions and delivery scope you accept after inspecting an actual result; and the organization and partial-response constraints for repair work. Adopt these constraints before they guide the work, connect them to actual source/subject and code/run references, and show their effect in the implementation and results. You may adopt an agent suggestion with your own source-grounded reason and constraint. Record an owned unresolved step where the evidence does not support completion, and reconsider affected choices when later evidence arrives. Concise statements in your normal conversation are enough; no separate decision register or fabricated mistake is required.\\n\\n\\nVerify the ordinary path and every material branch in the supplied records, including later corrections, cancellations and replay. Check quantities, identities, source bindings and state transitions as well as status labels. Additional isolated test inputs are allowed but do not replace the primary run. Document unrun checks and implementation limitations honestly; a case-count or time limit does not remove assigned work.\\nIssues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nHow do you organize the repair work in partial response constraints?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nYou can organize repair work either by per-claim packages or by grouping all missing-evidence items by the specific person responsible for supplying them. The key constraint is to retain each item's subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for tracking.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nWhat's the best way to adopt these constraints before they guide the work?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nYou can choose between per-claim packages or grouping items by the person responsible, provided you clearly track the subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for every single item.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:29 PM\\n\\nWhich one of those is the most difficult to maintain?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:29 PM\\n\\nBoth approaches have trade-offs; per-claim packages require less cross-referencing but result in more packages, whereas grouping by the person reduces the number of units but requires item-level matching and careful partial completion tracking.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nCan cases remain unresolved when the facts require it?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nYes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nWhat type of report will affect the work, reason, responsible person, and evidence needed to resume?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nYou can use any format, such as a per-claim package or a grouped task list, as long as it consistently retains the specific claim version, the missing evidence or fact, the responsible owner, and the next action required to resume.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"171a60\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.91575918,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":17,\"output\":\"Recorded 128 tracked file hashes and original untracked inventory\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a157fb-72d7-7143-a650-0e15b4d0e044","create_time":1792477591.8940232}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
