{"timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:51:23.361Z","ordinal":10657,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a157fb-72d7-7143-a650-0e15b4d0e044","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad70f60604481909b6b4c9f27a82f2c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Implemented locally on **`omega/project-d-attempt-3`**. Main remains at `653eec28484f601d6568dc55bf7b3db955dd2ce0`.\n\nThe new **`continue-repairs`** command addresses the original requirements for item-specific partial responses, verified evidence, affected-work revalidation, preserved history and operator resumption.\n\n| Supported | Explicitly unsupported |\n|---|---|\n| Receipt PDF and settled merchant-payment XLSX evidence | Approval, Finance-event, exception, policy and budget imports |\n| Current claim and correction evidence repairs | Split-payment/shared-cost changes |\n| Evidence requested by a retained reviewer return | Non-claim repairs and migration from receipt-only derived results |\n| Successive responses against derived results | Automatic reimbursement authorization or closure |\n\nConnected synthetic tests demonstrate:\n\n- Receipt-only delivery leaves A held; later merchant proof resolves its evidence repair.\n- B’s insufficient/invalid evidence stays open; unrelated C remains unchanged.\n- Returned work resumes expense checks but remains assigned for human re-review.\n- Current r2 repairs succeed; stale r1 responses reject.\n- Replacements retain superseded evidence.\n- Exact replay is inert; conflicting replay and tampered ancestry reject.\n- CSV, state, queue, report and unsent drafts agree; admitted cash remains unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** 589 full-suite tests passed; 58 focused tests passed; no failures. Git whitespace checks passed, including both new files. All **53 published evidence entries** match stored/restored hashes; **123 unaffected tracked files** match the start baseline. Historical untracked paths remain intact.\n\nLocal synthetic demonstration: [report.md](/tmp/project-d-attempt3-synthetic-dgvj65hg/shell-two/report.md).\n\nSeven changed files:\n\n- `README.md`\n- `skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md`\n- `src/travel_claim/cli.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/outputs.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/receipt_continuation.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/repair_continuation.py` — new\n- `tests/test_repair_continuation.py` — new\n\nNative Notion access remains blocked. No genuine stakeholder response or real financial closure is claimed. Derived results use built-in integrity checks, not full-run submission certification.\n\nElapsed: approximately **26 minutes**. Nothing staged, committed or published. Entire history remains preserved; a pre-existing finalized transcript tail was observed but not published or remotely checked."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792479072328,"completed_at_ms":1792479083361}}
